# Scavenger's Talent level 3: "At the beginning of your end step, you may sacrifice three other nonland permanents. If you
# do, return a creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield with a finality counter on it." Bot1 reaches level 3 in
# turn 5 (Level 2 in turn 3). At the end step it sacrifices its Healer's Hawk and two Moxen; the creature card may be one of
# the sacrificed permanents (the ruling), and the Hawk comes back with a finality counter on it, as a new object. The level-2
# ability triggers for each of the three sacrifices (three mills of two, all aimed at Bot2: 6 cards), and the level-1 ability
# for the Hawk's death makes a Food. Bot2 plays a land each turn so nothing is discarded.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Scavenger's Talent
Healer's Hawk
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x24

